biz\"\n data-hay=\"Tungsten&#x27;s Price Spike Is a Hundred-Year War Prediction Market: China Cuts Supply and It Goes Up Tenfold Tungsten&#x27;s supply-and-demand cycle behaves like a war prediction market: prices spike before wars and collapse after them. China controls eighty percent of supply, and the West could restart old mines for only tens of millions of dollars — but with no futures market, the projects are hard to finance. Odd Lots Odd Lots The Tungsten Market Is Warning of an Upcoming War Tungsten Critical Minerals Geopolitics Supply Chains Mining Investment War Economy Ammonium Paratungstate (APT) Dry Metric Ton Unit (DMTU) Tungsten Carbide Ionic Absorption Clays\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-03-oddlots-钨价暴涨背后-一场百年战争预测市场/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://www.omnycontent.com/d/playlist/e73c998e-6e60-432f-8610-ae210140c5b1/8a94442e-5a74-4fa2-8b8d-ae27003a8d6b/982f5071-765c-403d-969d-ae27003a8d83/image.jpg?t=1681322812&amp;size=Medium\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"O\"><span class=\"dur\">44:26</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Odd Lots</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0803</span></div>\n<h2>Tungsten&#x27;s Price Spike Is a Hundred-Year War Prediction Market: China Cuts Supply and It Goes Up Tenfold</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Tungsten&#x27;s supply-and-demand cycle behaves like a war prediction market: prices spike before wars and collapse after them. China controls eighty percent of supply, and the West could restart old mines for only tens of millions of dollars — but with no futures market, the projects are hard to finance.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Tungsten</span><span class=\"tag\">Critical Minerals</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"parent\"\n data-hay=\"The biggest financial gift to a child isn&#x27;t a college fund — it&#x27;s a business at 10 A 10-year-old earned $759 of retirement money from pet-sitting — not early hothousing, but real responsibility building systems thinking, boundaries, persistence and financial independence. Your Parenting Mojo Your Parenting Mojo Re-release: Raising an Entrepreneur (Without Taking Over Their Business) Kid entrepreneurship Financial literacy Roth IRA Self-directed learning Neurodiversity Hands-off parenting Roth IRA unschooling sliding scale pricing guide on the side intake form\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-03-parentmojo-给孩子最大的财务礼物不是大学基金-是让她10岁创业/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://artwork.captivate.fm/12802a36-dbca-4912-a62e-cbce5aacddb8/podcast-cover-your-parenting-mojo-03-01-copy.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"Y\"><span class=\"dur\">1:00:19</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"parent\"><span class=\"src\">Your Parenting Mojo</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0803</span></div>\n<h2>The biggest financial gift to a child isn&#x27;t a college fund — it&#x27;s a business at 10</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">A 10-year-old earned $759 of retirement money from pet-sitting — not early hothousing, but real responsibility building systems thinking, boundaries, persistence and financial independence.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Kid entrepreneurship</span><span class=\"tag\">Financial literacy</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\"\n data-hay=\"Regulating America&#x27;s Own AI Is Pointless Unless China&#x27;s Open Models Are Curbed Too If the US restrains only its own frontier models without suppressing China&#x27;s open models, the safety logic does not hold; the real decider is the compute stock and the ability to deliver. ChinaTalk ChinaTalk Jordan talks AI with Sebastian Mallaby on his show &#x27;The Spillover&#x27; US-China AI race Open weights Compute AI safety Export controls DeepSeek open weights distillation alignment tokenomics frontier lab\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-01-chinatalk-美国要慢可以-但得把中国开源一起管住/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://megaphone.imgix.net/podcasts/618c3788-8da9-11f1-af6c-d70cf8df26ec/image/a5b996295467b1c63c192faa561b2fcb.jpeg?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;max-w=3000&amp;max-h=3000&amp;fit=crop&amp;auto=format,compress&amp;w=400&amp;auto=format\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"C\"><span class=\"dur\">1:20:03</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\">ChinaTalk</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0801</span></div>\n<h2>Regulating America&#x27;s Own AI Is Pointless Unless China&#x27;s Open Models Are Curbed Too</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">If the US restrains only its own frontier models without suppressing China&#x27;s open models, the safety logic does not hold; the real decider is the compute stock and the ability to deliver.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">US-China AI race</span><span class=\"tag\">Open weights</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\"\n data-hay=\"Feishu and DingTalk Exit; the Personal Agent Takes Over AI Office Work Feishu is being folded into Doubao and DingTalk is ceding ground to Qwen Office (千问办公); enterprise IM has finished its historical mission. The center of AI office work shifts from organizational collaboration to individual productivity, with coding as the Agent&#x27;s foundation. 乱翻书 乱翻书 270.大厂押注AI办公，飞书和钉钉却先成了配角 AI Office Work Feishu DingTalk ByteDance Tencent Agents Agent ARR (Annual Recurring Revenue) CAPEX (Capital Expenditure) GEO (Generative Engine Optimization)\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-01-luanfanshu-飞书钉钉退场-ai办公的主角成了个人agent/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://image.xyzcdn.net/Fqw6Nl1IrcV-q1AhWjdN-AhunBH8.jpg?imageMogr2/thumbnail/400x/format/webp\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"乱\"><span class=\"dur\">1:37:09</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">乱翻书</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0801</span></div>\n<h2>Feishu and DingTalk Exit; the Personal Agent Takes Over AI Office Work</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Feishu is being folded into Doubao and DingTalk is ceding ground to Qwen Office (<span lang=\"zh\">千问办公</span>); enterprise IM has finished its historical mission. The center of AI office work shifts from organizational collaboration to individual productivity, with coding as the Agent&#x27;s foundation.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>4</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI Office Work</span><span class=\"tag\">Feishu</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\"\n data-hay=\"Dissected and Displayed After Hanging: What She Threatened Was Order, Not Money Mary Bateman, an 18th-century fraudster, worked through fortune-telling and a poisoned pie — not for the money, but for the pleasure of control. Her cons landed precisely on what people wanted to believe, and after her death her body was still put on display, exposing how much a society feared anyone who upended its order. Cautionary Tales with Tim Harford Cautionary Tales Arsenic and Lace: The Trial of the Yorkshire Witch - with Maddy Pelling Scams Psychological manipulation 18th century Historical crime Fraud defence Desire for power pleading the belly bottle conjurer ill wishes / well wishes\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-31-cautionary-约克郡女巫罪案-骗局的核心是权力欲/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://www.omnycontent.com/d/playlist/e73c998e-6e60-432f-8610-ae210140c5b1/c0ae8c6e-22f0-4e9b-ac1c-ae390037ac53/7f5a4714-6b10-4ccf-a424-ae390037ac70/image.jpg?t=1650471153&amp;size=Medium\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"C\"><span class=\"dur\">43:31</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">Cautionary Tales with Tim Harford</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0731</span></div>\n<h2>Dissected and Displayed After Hanging: What She Threatened Was Order, Not Money</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Mary Bateman, an 18th-century fraudster, worked through fortune-telling and a poisoned pie — not for the money, but for the pleasure of control. Her cons landed precisely on what people wanted to believe, and after her death her body was still put on display, exposing how much a society feared anyone who upended its order.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Scams</span><span class=\"tag\">Psychological manipulation</span>\n</div></div></a>"]
